# Inner product over oneDNN's CI shapes (ip/shapes_ci).
#
# The brgemm inner product (brgemm:rvv) takes forward, 2D, OC >= 16, IC >= 64
# without attributes, in f32, bf16 and f16 (with an f16 dst for f16). The PR
# blocks the weights left to the primitive by the kernel's M tile and keeps
# the MB/OC cache guards for plain weights only; mb 1, 4 and 32 sit on both
# sides of them. ba user weights are still accepted. ab weights, which it
# declines, go to the gemm inner product (gemm:rvv, f32, on the rvjit sgemm).

--reset
--dt=f32,bf16:bf16:f32,f16:f16:f32,f16:f16:f16
--dir=FWD_B
--mb=1,4,32
--stag=any --dtag=any
--wtag=any,ba,ab
--batch=shapes_ci
